801: Thus, we may further assume that~\begin{math}
802: t = k \geq 3
803: \end{math}.
804: 
805: We have previously noted that the problem belongs to NP.
806: The transformation is from $t$-colouring.
807: Suppose an instance of $t$-colouring, a simple, undirected graph $G$ is given.
808: We will replace each edge of $G$ by the oriented graph  which we now construct.
809: 
810: Let $C$ be the directed cycle of length $t$ with vertex sequence~\begin{math}
811: v_0, v_1, \ldots, v_{t-1}, v_0
812: \end{math}.
813: Add four new vertices~\begin{math}
814: x_0, x_1, y_0, y_1
815: \end{math}, and arcs to make the directed paths
816: \begin{math}
817: x_0, x_1, v_1
818: \end{math} and~\begin{math}
819: y_0, y_1, v_2
820: \end{math}.
821: This completes the construction of $F$.
822: Observe that $x_0$ is joined to every vertex of $C$ except $v_0$ by a directed path of length at most $t$.
823: Every vertex of $C$ is assigned a different colour in a $k$-dipath $t$-colouring of $F$.
824: Hence, the vertices $x_0$ and $v_0$ must be assigned the same colour.
825: Similarly, the vertices $y_0$ and $v_1$ must be assigned the same colour.
826: In particular, $x_0$ and $y_0$ must be assigned different colours.
827: Furthermore, any assignment of two different colours to $x_0$ and $y_0$ can be extended to a 
828: $k$-dipath $t$-colouring of $F$.
829: 
830: Construct an oriented graph $G^\prime$ from $G$ as follows. 
831: Replace each edge $xy$ of $G$ with a copy $F_{xy}$ of $F$ by 
832: identifying $x_0$ with $x$ and $y_0$ with $y$.
833: The construction can clearly be carried out in polynomial time.
834: Observe that each vertex in~\begin{math}
835: V(G) \cap V(G^\prime)
836: \end{math} has in-degree 0.
837: 
838: We claim that $G$ is $t$-colourable if and only if $G^\prime$ has a $k$-dipath $t$-colouring.
839: Suppose that a $t$-colouring of $G$ is given.
840: For each copy of $F$ in $G^\prime$, this assignment gives different colours to $x_0$ and $y_0$.

