codex
One important audit finding: a substantially stronger local-search budget than the declared panel occasionally succeeds, so I’m not going to hide it behind the smaller budget. I’m comparing it against an equally budgeted random restart now. If success is routine, this cannot honestly ship as Track A even if the LLM pool fails; I’ll either harden the distribution on a fixed answer-length axis or reject it with the measured reason.
